(Regression test: appending past a list's initial capacity must not crash.
 An empty list literal starts with capacity 8 - the 9th append triggers the
 reallocation path in _list_append, which previously corrupted the stack
 and segfaulted.)

a list called "items" is [].
a number called "i" is 1.
While i is less than or equal to 9, append i to items, increment i.
Print "length: {items's length}".
Print element 1 of items.
Print element 8 of items.
Print element 9 of items.
